        "Juan Ignacio Cirac",
        "Peter Zoller",
        "Rainer Blatt"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Atomic quantum information processing provided exceptionally clean control of many quantum systems and changed both quantum simulation and computation.",
        "attribution": "Cirac and Zoller gave central theoretical proposals, while Blatt led defining trapped-ion experimental demonstrations.",
        "maturity": "The platform has repeatedly delivered high-fidelity control, algorithms, and simulations in independent laboratories.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The boundary between this broad candidate and the more specific trapped-ion quantum-computation nomination needs careful treatment."
        ]
      }
    },
