        "Jun Ye"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks transformed precision measurement through unprecedented stability, accuracy, and broad physical reach.",
        "attribution": "Katori originated the magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept and Ye made complementary, decisive experimental advances.",
        "maturity": "The clocks are a mature international technology with compelling reproducibility and scientific applications.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "A future redefinition of the second is not itself the basis for a physics prize."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
